 Identity scheme 2 reserves `java:package:<qualified-name>` for package inventory nodes, avoiding collision with `java:<qualified-type>` when one source set contains both a type and an identically named package. Type/member source signatures retain their existing form. This is an explicit canonicalization correction: old immutable catalog documents and hashes remain untouched, old package overlay/grant keys are not automatically aliased or retargeted, and publication must quarantine any identity-kind ambiguity until owner reconciliation. Package nodes are discovery-only and never executable. `test_package_and_type_have_distinct_identity_namespaces` reproduces and guards the collision.
 
