+## Current reviewed-candidate pipeline
+
+The copied source pipeline supports pinned Java-source JSONL caches and current SDK lifecycle-index caches. Java declarations and JVM index entries have separate identities until conservative equivalence is proven. Java wildcard/import/type-variable/inheritance semantics and index-absent types/constants remain unknown where unproven. Dependencies are pinned in requirements-extraction.txt; no dependency installation was performed by this task. Point positions use tuple indexing; the diagnosed binding getter defect is distinct from the inferred connection to the prior exact crash.
+
+aidl_members.py inventories structured parcelable/union fields, enumerants and interface constants as source metadata, preserving raw initializers and unknown syntax. Declaration ordinals are never asserted as wire tags. Imported runtime types, wire layouts/codecs, generated transactions and device reachability remain separate unresolved facts. This helper does not modify the Java cache parser.
+
+Round004 reproduction evidence was evidence/tests-regression-024.txt (85 tests) and evidence/legacy-populated-current-schema-validation.json (135508 legacy entries; storage validation passes, semantic rebuild false,552 variant omissions). That historical snapshot had release004 staging. Current production progress and independent validation are recorded separately in the latest progress evidence; old snapshot scores are not current production assessments. Acquisition100% of selected paths does not establish all-current-bindings coverage across985 excluded repositories.
+
+
+Identity canonicalization v2 covers all source languages: java:owner#method(normalizedTypes), java:owner#field and java:package:qualified.package; java-source: uses the same source-spelled forms (including java-source:package:); aidl:descriptor#method(normalizedTypes), aidl:descriptor#field and aidl:descriptor type roots; jvm:binary/Owner and jvm:binary/Owner#name(JVM-argument-descriptors)JVM-return-descriptor, with jvm:binary/Owner#fieldName where the lifecycle index omits a field descriptor. SHA-256 hashes the complete prefixed string. These remain distinct IDs until explicit proven equivalence is recorded in extensions.proven_current_sdk_jvm_identity; equivalence never silently retargets grants. AIDL parcelable/union/enum roots use additive1.1.0 kinds aidl-parcelable/aidl-union/aidl-enum with unknown wire codecs, not unsupported-source labels after successful declaration parsing.
+
+New owner mutation reasons live in entry_history_reasons, an append-only sidecar keyed to the immutable history revision. HistoryEvent.reason is optional for legacy/system records only; every Mutation reason must be inserted atomically with its corresponding history. Registry.api_level may be null when applicability is not established.
+
+
+Signature reconciliation is a source-line no-drop guard, not an independently established semantic member count. Its lexer includes unsupported nonblank declaration lines; a mutant extractor dropping a fixture method fails publication. Grammar correctness uses targeted golden fixtures; actual current SDK membership is separately evidenced by the official lifecycle index, not inferred from this same line filter. Missing source/SDK semantics and production coverage remain explicit gaps. See tests-regression-027.txt and the latest finding ledger; no self-score is claimed.
+
+
+Index type declarations use additive1.1.0 kind type with type_kind_status unknown, separating known type presence from unknown class/interface/annotation semantics. The latest schemas use1.1.0 IDs and gate new type/AIDL kinds to1.1+ (including minor10+), rejecting those kinds in1.0 documents. Published/validated/retired/rejected registry membership and source links are sealed; copy migration loads staged memberships, restores terminal states, then installs pointers through all collision/base guards. A deleted local tombstone colliding with a new import requires explicit conflict just like an active local addition.
